# Playwright Constitution

Non-negotiable defaults for this repo. Details live in skills; this is the checklist.

## MUST

| Rule | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| Role-based locators | Prefer `getByRole` → label/placeholder → text → `getByTestId` (comment why). Locators live in POM only. |
| Web-first assertions | Auto-retrying `expect(locator)...`; never `waitForTimeout` or manual sleeps. |
| `storageState` auth | Reuse saved auth; do not log in inside specs. |
| Unique self-cleaning data | Faker/unique names; every create tears down (API cleanup). |
| One tag per test | Exactly one of `@smoke` · `@sanity` · `@regression` · `@api` · `@e2e` · `@destructive` on each `test(...)`, never on `describe`. `@destructive` only for shared/global state (locale/roles/flags/settings); run serial + `afterEach`/`afterAll` revert. Own-data cleanup keeps an importance tag. |

## SHOULD

| Rule | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| Faker factories | Build test data via factories/helpers, not inline literals. |
| Enums for repeated strings | Shared UI/copy/status strings → enums or constants. |
| JSDoc on action methods | Document POM actions (intent + notable waits/side effects). |

## WON'T

| Never | Why |
|-------|-----|
| XPath / brittle CSS | Breaks on markup churn; use role-based locators. |
| `waitForTimeout` | Flaky and slow; use web-first expects. |
| Hardcoded secrets | Credentials/tokens only via env / auth setup. |
| `any` | Keep TypeScript strict; type fixtures and helpers. |
| Weakened assertions | Do not delete/soften `expect` to go green. |
| Healing a real bug | App defects → `bug-reporter`; heal locators only after triage says drift. |
| Tags on `describe` | Tag individual tests only. |

## Agent governance

Behavioral contract (not hook-enforced). **Audit, then edit.**

### Proposal (before any non-trivial edit)

Emit this block first; do not edit until the confidence rule below allows it:

```markdown
## Proposal
- **Scope:** <files / flows touched>
- **Confidence:** <1–10>
- **Rationale:** <why this approach>
- **Unknowns:** <missing facts, or "none">
```

### Confidence gate

| Score | Action |
|-------|--------|
| `< 5` | Do **not** proceed. Ask for the missing input. |
| `5–7` | Proceed only with **explicit Unknowns** listed **and** human approval. |
| `≥ 8` | Proceed. |

### Never invent

Do not invent a path, enum, env var, credential, or UI/API message. **Ask** or **explore** (live app / repo / docs) instead.

